<title>USA: Wisconsin, Michigan get new welfare funding.</title>
<headline>Wisconsin, Michigan get new welfare funding.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wisconsin and Michigan have been approved to become the first states to receive funding under the nation's new welfare law, the White House announced on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;I congratulate both states for recognising what all Americans agree on: welfare is first and foremost about work,&quot; Clinton said in a statement.</p>
<p>Under the plans submitted by the two states, a five-year limit will be imposed on recipients -- as required by the law recently signed by Clinton.</p>
</text>
